<title>USA: US mortgage rates rose in week - Freddie Mac.</title>
<headline>US mortgage rates rose in week - Freddie Mac.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average commitment rate on U.S. 30-year fixed rate mortgages rose slightly to 7.97 percent in the week ended March 28, from 7.94 percent in the previous week, Freddie Mac said Thursday.</p>
<p>For 15-year fixed-rate loans, the rate rose to 7.48 percent in the latest week from 7.45 percent in the prior week.</p>
<p>The average commitment rate for one-year adjustable-rate mortgages remained unchanged from last week at 5.71 percent.</p>
